{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Farhan has a blue hat, a white hat, a blue scarf, a white scarf, and a green scarf. He randomly chooses one hat and one scarf. What is the probability that the hat and the scarf are the same colour? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bdadd0067a9e6f078ac90a7d8e0a01050d2e1868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{5}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{3}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{3}{5}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{6}  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"404\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability for the scarf and hat to have the same colour in the second step in each case for the hat colour. Thus, there must be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dabbc555637252d1dad381cc8c11e2f6bada7f41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" /> probability of the hat and scarf being the same colour because the probabilities match, regardless of what colour the hat is.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the scarves can lead to the same colour because there is no green hat and both have the same probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of having the same colour, so the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba6acba31d74426b828605fb4e8a978c92c2d84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dabbc555637252d1dad381cc8c11e2f6bada7f41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&am